// S6.1 unknown layout qualifier — FIXED 2026-10-14:
// `layout(q77 = 64)` now rejects at parse time ('q77' : unrecognized layout identifier taking an
// assigned value) instead of silently changing nothing. The whitelist covers everything the corpus
// uses plus the spec's other stage primitives, image formats, XFB modes, ray-tracing payload
// qualifiers, and depth/stencil/fragment-ordering modes. Stage-scoped misuse (local_size_x in a
// fragment shader) is deliberately not checked — the parser is context-free; glslang rejects that
// separately ("for this stage").
// Expected today: REJECT (fixed).
#version 460
layout(q77 = 64) in;
void main(){}